## A monolithic kernel designed to power blurOS

Syscall docs:

To initiate a system call, they take 3 max arguments in rbx, rcx, and rdx. The syscall handler is 0x30 (48), the steps to initiate are:

1. Set RAX to the target syscall
2. Set RBX, RCX, RDX to your arguments (sometimes not all or none or all are needed)
3. Use the int $0x30 instruction
4. Set your variable to RAX if it isn't listed as void after the interrupt

Current System Call Signatures (form of copy/direct returntype RAX(args))
- 0(char* rbx) / direct void print(char* string)

- 1(uint32_t rbx) / direct void clear_screen(uint32_t color)

- 2(char* rbx) / copy char* kscan(char* buf)

- 3(void (*)() rbx, int rcx, char *rdx) / direct void create_proc(void (*)() func, int pid, char* pname)

Warning: sleep is NOT_IMPL due to hang

- 4(uint64_t rbx) / direct void sleep(uint64_t ms)

- 5() / direct void print_currently_running_proc()

- 6(char* rbx, void* rcx, uint32_t rdx) / copy void* hr_read(char* filename, void* buffer, uint32_t size)

- 7(uint64_t rbx) / copy void* alloc(uint64_t size)

- 8(char* rbx) / direct int open(char* filename)

- 9(int rbx, char* rcx, uint32_t rdx) / direct int read(int fd, char* buf, uint32_t len)

- 10(int rbx) / direct int close(int fd)

- 11(int rbx, int rcx, int rdx) / direct int lseek(int fd, int offset, int whence)

- 12(char* rbx) / direct int vfs_get_filesize(char* name)


rest isn't documented yet (hopefully by tommorow lol!)